<title>▶ Samir Subberwal is the global head of wealth solutions at Standard Chartered bank. @stanchartin ...</title>
<link>https://www.instagram.com/p/DgFAt40znhK/</link>
<guid isPermaLink="false">instagram:https://www.instagram.com/p/DgFAt40znhK/</guid>
<pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 09:07:34 GMT</pubDate>
<dc:creator>Sonia Shenoy · Instagram</dc:creator>
<category>Instagram</category>
<media:content url="https://www.instagram.com/p/DgFAt40znhK/media?size=l" medium="image"/>
<description><![CDATA[<video controls><source src="" poster="https://www.instagram.com/p/DgFAt40znhK/media?size=l" type="video/mp4"><img src="https://www.instagram.com/p/DgFAt40znhK/media?size=l" alt=""></video><br><br>Samir Subberwal is the global head of wealth solutions at Standard Chartered bank.  @stanchartin <br />
<br />
Standard Chartered bank recently upgraded their house view on Gold, stating that it looks attractive post the recent fall. <br />
<br />
As of Nov 22nd 2026, Gold prices have crashed to 14 month lows <br />
<br />
Gold is now at 1.25 lakhs per 10 grams<br />
which is a 31% fall from january highs of 1.8 lakhs <br />
<br />
silver is worse off, down 65% from jan highs <br />
<br />
gold is falling mainly because the market expects the fed to raise interest rates. <br />
also gold is priced in dollars so a stronger dollar makes it costlier for the rest of the world <br />
<br />
Full episode with Samir Subberwal of Standard Chartered bank out this week on @themoneymindset.co ✨]]></description>
